IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- War Crimes Act 1945 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1945A00048.txt (compilation No. 5, 23
-- May 2018). The accused asks: "Is what I am said to have done a serious crime
-- and a war crime under the Act; can I be charged; what is the most I can get;
-- do I have a defence?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 6(1)(a)-(k), (4)-(5): the kind of act.
DECLARE `Act kind` IS ONE OF
    `murder, manslaughter, grievous bodily harm, wounding, rape, indecent assault or abduction, or a variant or complicity in one`
    `deporting or interning a person in a death camp, slave labour camp or like place, or complicity in it`
    `another act`

-- s 7(1), (3): the connection with the war or occupation.
DECLARE `Connection` IS ONE OF
    `in the course of hostilities in a war`
    `in the course of an occupation`
    `in pursuing a war or occupation policy`
    `on behalf of a power at war or occupying`
    `in persecution or genocide, in a country at war or occupied`
    `only incidental or remote`

DECLARE `War crime case` HAS
    `the act`                                                       IS A `Act kind`
    -- s 6(1)-(3): an offence under Australian law then (by analogy if abroad),
    -- allowing for any defence available under that law
    `it was such an offence under the law then in force in part of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the connection`                                                IS A `Connection`
    -- s 5 war: in Europe between 1 September 1939 and 8 May 1945
    `it was in Europe`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was done on`                                                IS A DATE
    -- s 10
    `it involved the wilful killing of a person`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 11
    `I am an Australian citizen or resident`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 17
    `it was permitted by the laws, customs and usages of war`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was a crime against humanity under international law`       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `War crime position` HAS
    `a serious crime under s 6`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a war crime under s 7`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an offence under the Act`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `chargeable under s 11`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I may be imprisoned for life`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment in years otherwise`                       IS A NUMBER
    `a laws-of-war defence under s 17`                              IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 6(1), (3): a listed offence under Australian law; s 6(4)-(5): deportation
-- or internment in a death or slave labour camp, whatever the local law said
-- (s 6(6)).
@ref s 6
GIVEN c IS A `War crime case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a serious crime` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `the act`
    WHEN `deporting or interning a person in a death camp, slave labour camp or like place, or complicity in it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another act` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE c's `it was such an offence under the law then in force in part of Australia`

-- s 5 war: in Europe, 1 September 1939 to 8 May 1945.
@ref s 5 war, s 9(1)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `War crime case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it was in the war period` c IF
        c's `it was done on` AT LEAST Date 1 9 1939
    AND c's `it was done on` AT MOST Date 8 5 1945

-- s 7(1)-(3): connected with the war or occupation, not merely incidentally.
@ref s 7
GIVEN c IS A `War crime case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a war crime` c IF
        `it is a serious crime` c
    AND c's `it was in Europe`
    AND `it was in the war period` c
    AND NOT (c's `the connection` EQUALS `only incidental or remote`)

@ref s 9(1)
GIVEN c IS A `War crime case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an offence` c IF `it is a war crime` c

-- s 17: permitted by the laws of war and not a crime against humanity; s 16:
-- superior orders are no defence.
@ref ss 16, 17
GIVEN c IS A `War crime case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the laws of war are a defence` c IF
        c's `it was permitted by the laws, customs and usages of war`
    AND NOT (c's `it was a crime against humanity under international law`)

-- s 11: only Australian citizens or residents may be charged.
@ref s 11
GIVEN c IS A `War crime case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may be charged` c IF
        `it is an offence` c
    AND c's `I am an Australian citizen or resident`

-- s 10: life for wilful killing; otherwise 25 years.
@ref s 10
GIVEN c IS A `War crime case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the other maximum for` c MEANS
    IF `it is an offence` c AND NOT (c's `it involved the wilful killing of a person`) THEN 25 ELSE 0

@ref ss 5-11, 16-17
@export default The position of a person accused under the War Crimes Act 1945 (Cth): whether the act is a serious crime (murder, manslaughter, grievous bodily harm, wounding, rape, indecent assault, abduction, or variants or complicity, as offences under the law then in force in part of Australia, or deportation or internment in a death or slave labour camp: s 6); whether it is a war crime (in Europe from 1 September 1939 to 8 May 1945, in the course of hostilities or occupation, in pursuit of a war or occupation policy, on behalf of a power at war, or in persecution or genocide, but not merely incidentally: ss 5, 7, 9); whether they may be charged (only Australian citizens or residents: s 11); the most they can get (life for wilful killing, otherwise 25 years: s 10); and whether the laws of war are a defence (s 17; superior orders are not: s 16). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `War crime case`  @desc The act, its status under Australian law then, its connection with the war, where and when, whether it was a killing, my citizenship or residence, and the laws-of-war facts
GIVETH A `War crime position`
`the war crime position for` c MEANS
    `War crime position` OF `it is a serious crime` c, `it is a war crime` c, `it is an offence` c, `I may be charged` c,
                            `it is an offence` c AND c's `it involved the wilful killing of a person`, `the other maximum for` c,
                            `the laws of war are a defence` c
